<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#deflation">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deflation</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as deflationary</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Deflation is a sustained fall in the general level of prices, often linked to a shortage of money. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>-based monetary economy depended on silver imports, and their disruption in the early nineteenth century produced deflationary pressures that worsened fiscal strain and weakened provincial administration.</p></div>
